# A forgotten `|` between two operators on one line: DS0102, with a fix that inserts it.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | where amount > 10 project customerId, amount
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..65
  PIPELINE@0..64
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    WHERE_OP@20..37
      IDENT@20..25 "where"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      BIN_EXPR@26..37
        NAME_REF@26..32
          IDENT@26..32 "amount"
        WHITESPACE@32..33 " "
        GT@33..34 ">"
        WHITESPACE@34..35 " "
        LITERAL@35..37
          LONG@35..37 "10"
    WHITESPACE@37..38 " "
    PROJECT_OP@38..64
      IDENT@38..45 "project"
      WHITESPACE@45..46 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@46..56
        NAME_REF@46..56
          IDENT@46..56 "customerId"
      COMMA@56..57 ","
      WHITESPACE@57..58 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@58..64
        NAME_REF@58..64
          IDENT@58..64 "amount"
  WHITESPACE@64..65 "\n"

error[DS0102]: missing `|` before `project`
  --> query:1:39
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | where amount > 10 project customerId, amount
  |                                       ^^^^^^^ `project` starts a new operator
  |
  = help: insert `|` to pipe into `project`: `| project`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | where amount > 10 | project customerId, amount
which parses without errors
